{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"role":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The four rules","anchor":"The-four-rules"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Flag, don’t fake","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"title":"Drag"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"title":"Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Interaction","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","role":"symbol"}}}